Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:52:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] fix(desktop): ISO arm is found by policy, dated and
 captioned correctly

Review findings on the replayed ISO-2 + SLAC research arm:

- The leaderboard fingerprint skipped every rule-armed benchmark, so without
  a sidecar artifact id (web build, older sidecar, before /health answers)
  the ISO edition fell back to the 2026-09-12 grid under a "not measured"
  caption for the very policy its benchmark used. policyArm() maps a
  detection policy to its research arm (none -> baseline, SLAC -> empirical /
  normative, ISO-2 -> iso2, both -> iso2normative), and the fingerprint now
  compares against that arm.
- The evidence tile said the v4 set was "Not replayed" next to a replayed
  arm; it now says what is actually missing: the SLAC projection was not
  checked against a replay.
- Grids can date an arm separately (armScoredAt); the ISO arm shows its own
  2026-09-30 rescoring date instead of the rest of the v4 grid's.
- An unavailable arm choice falls back to the edition's policy arm first.
- The ISO_EDITION test fixture carries the edition's real leaderboard.

Tests: 16 files / 301 pass; tsc adds no error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
